A second, completely separate `AdminController` is added later, and it calls `ticketService.issueTicket(...)` directly (it does not go through the original `TicketController`). Will the "gate must be ENTRY" rule still be enforced for requests coming from `AdminController`?

int totalPaid = bill.getPayments().stream()
        .filter(p -> p.getPaymentStatus() == PaymentStatus.SUCCESS)
        .mapToInt(Payment::getAmount)
        .sum();
if (totalPaid >= bill.getAmount()) {
    bill.setBillStatus(BillStatus.PAID);
}
A `Bill` has `amount = 500`. Two `Payment` records exist on it: Payment1 (amount=200, status=SUCCESS) and Payment2 (amount=300, status=FAILED). What is `totalPaid`, and what happens to the bill's status?

